From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yu Wei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:44:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Break lines after soft hyphens with a hyphen

A line broken after a soft hyphen (U+00AD) ended with nothing: the
opportunity was like any other. CSS hyphens draws a hyphen there, counts
it in whether the line fits, and with hyphens: none has no opportunity.
StyleProperty::SoftHyphens (SoftHyphens; TextStyle::soft_hyphens, Break
by default, which keeps upstream's behaviour) gives NoBreak for none (an
emergency opportunity at most, as overflow-wrap gives one) and
Hyphen(advance) for the others, with the advance of the hyphen the
embedder shapes and draws.

parley_engine marks soft hyphens (CharacterFlags::is_soft_hyphen, cached
as ShapedCluster::is_soft_hyphen). The line breaker takes the
opportunity after one as its style has it, an inline's start edge taking
it too (an atomic inline's own opportunities are its own): with the
hyphen at the line's end where it fits, or where the line has no
opportunity before it. LineMetrics::hyphen_advance is then the part of
the line's advance that is the hyphen; in an RTL paragraph the line's
items leave room for it on the left of offset. The min/max-content
measurer counts the hyphen at the end of the fragment it ends.
